# Invention No. 2 in C minor, BWV 773 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: grave and closely argued, a strict canon at the octave.
# The subject is a long, winding sixteenth-note line over two bars
# (after an eighth rest); the bass follows the top exactly, two bars
# behind, for the first ten bars, and then the roles change and the top
# follows the bass. It wants a steady, sober pulse with room for the
# trills, never hurried.
#
# Time signature: 4/4, 27 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI.
# The top starts after an eighth rest inside bar 1 and the MIDI keeps
# that rest, so bar numbers match the score and no pickup is needed.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 58, 108 quarters, about 1:55.
# Track times: Andras Schiff (ECM, clavichord, Stage+ listing) 1:51,
# about 58; Gustav Leonhardt (harpsichord, Apple Music reissue) 2:03,
# about 53; Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, her own discography page) 1:27,
# about 74; Glenn Gould (Sony, 1964, High Res Audio listing) 2:54,
# about 37, a famously slow, deliberate outlier not followed. 58 is
# Schiff's tempo, between Leonhardt and Hewitt.
#
# Structure (read from the Mutopia score and checked against the MIDI;
# the canon was verified note for note: bass 3-10 = top 1-8, and top
# 13-22 = bass 11-20; the key plan is my own reading):
#   1-2    Subject, top, alone, C minor.
#   3-10   The bass follows in canon at the octave, two bars behind;
#          the top's line moves to E-flat major (5-8) and on toward
#          G minor.
#   11-12  Second half: the canon restarts with the bass leading,
#          subject in G minor.
#   13-22  The top follows the bass, two bars behind; B-flat and F
#          major (15-18), then back toward C minor (19-22, bass free).
#   23-24  Subject returns, top, C minor (as bars 1-2).
#   25-26  Subject, bottom, C minor, while the top runs to the close.
#   27     Final C, bare octave (no Picardy third), with a fermata.

tempo 58

voice mid 0          # two voices only: there is no middle voice to set back

dyn 1 mf             # bars 1-10: the first canon, C minor to E-flat
lead 3-4 bottom      # the canon entry in the bass (bars 1-2 the top alone)
broaden 10 0.94      # bar 10: a breath into G minor and the second half

dyn 11 mp            # bars 11-18: the roles change, the bass leads;
                     # a softer manual for the second half's start
lead 11-12 bottom    # subject, bass, G minor
lead 13-14 top       # subject, top, G minor, following the bass

ramp 19-22 f         # bars 19-22: the bass breaks free of the canon and
                     # works back to C minor, the one long build

lead 23-24 top       # bars 23-27 stay at f: the subject returns, top
lead 25-26 bottom    # subject, bass, into the final cadence

rit 2 0.7            # bar 26 into the final held C
